@tradition sowing
// Sowing morning: the sample tradition for wave 1a (the traditions engineer). The seasons designer owns it from here
// and may change anything. Format: plans/trad-format.md.
k: 434
title: Sowing morning
when: quarter week 1 saturday
at: 11:45-12:40
min: 20
prio: 1
where: 3 pool garden
hold: none
who: gardener 90%, garden-lover 75%, everyone 30%
anim: water
from: brennan
ties: garden sow

== mail
- A new season starts in the garden: Sowing morning tomorrow, 11:45, after the harvest. Everyone plants a seedling. Yours grows as long as you're aboard.

== ask
- Sowing morning today. Bring clean hands.
- I'm planting basil this time. Don't tell Brennan, she'll want it.   #funny

== here
- Two seeds a pot. One for luck.
- Gently. They're only small.   #warm

== thanks
- You press a seedling into its pot and write your name on the tag. {season} has begun.

== chatter
- Whose seedling is that, already leaning towards the lamps?   #funny
